---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & Product Philosophy | Charlie Herbozo-Vidal (New York, NY)"
  description="Product design and systems philosophy of Charlie Herbozo-Vidal, Principal Product Designer based in NYC. Solving complex product problems at the intersection of systems architecture, behavioral strategy, and emerging technology."
  image="/images/headshot.jpg"
  passwordProtected={false}
>
  <div class="about-page-wrap">
    <!-- Breadcrumb / Back Link -->
    <a href="/" class="back-link">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M19 12H5M12 19l-7-7 7-7" /></svg>
      Back to Systems &amp; Work
    </a>

    <!-- Executive Bio Section -->
    <header class="about-header">
      <div class="about-intro-grid">
        <div class="about-photo-col">
          <img src="/images/headshot.jpg" alt="Charlie Herbozo-Vidal" class="about-photo" />
          <div class="about-photo-badge">
            <span class="badge-dot"></span> Based in NYC • By way of Lima, Peru
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-bio-col">
          <span class="about-eyebrow">About Me</span>
          <h1 class="about-name">Charlie Herbozo-Vidal</h1>
          <p class="about-title-role">Principal Product Designer &amp; Systems Strategist</p>

          <p class="about-lead-text">
            I lead product design at the intersection of complex systems, behavioral strategy, and emerging technology.
          </p>

          <p>
            With roots in industrial design, I view software through an architectural lens: digital products are functional tools that must perform under real-world physical and cognitive pressures. Over the past several years at CVS Health, I’ve led design strategy across enterprise platforms: modernizing nationwide retail infrastructure, scaling an 80M-member loyalty ecosystem, and pioneering internal AI tooling.
          </p>

          <p>
            Whether aligning design tokens with production code or untangling legacy mainframe debt, I focus on turning messy, high-friction systems into products that are intuitive for users and undeniably profitable for the business.
          </p>

          <div class="about-contact-links">
            <a href="mailto:charlie@charliehv.design" class="btn-primary-about">Connect by Email</a>
            <a href="http://www.linkedin.com/in/charlie-herbozovidal" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-secondary-about">LinkedIn Profile &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Leadership Philosophy Section -->
    <section class="leadership-section">
      <div class="section-header-block text-center">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Core Philosophy</span>
        <h2 class="section-heading">How I Approach Product &amp; Systems Design</h2>
        <p class="section-subtext">
          The best product design happens when systems thinking, technical feasibility, and human psychology are treated as a single discipline.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="philosophy-grid">
        <div class="philosophy-card">
          <div class="philosophy-icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Systems Grounded in Reality</h3>
          <p>
            A system is only as good as how it behaves under real-world constraints, including hardware limitations, network latency, and user stress. I look beyond the canvas to design products that are durable, maintainable, and built to perform at production scale.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="philosophy-card">
          <div class="philosophy-icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="12" y1="1" x2="12" y2="23"/><path d="M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Design as a Driver of Business Value</h3>
          <p>
            Design should be accountable to the numbers leadership tracks. Whether unlocking $300M in operational efficiency or optimizing margin for an 80M-member ecosystem, I align user advocacy with quantifiable commercial outcomes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="philosophy-card">
          <div class="philosophy-icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="2"/><rect x="9" y="9" width="6" height="6"/><line x1="9" y1="1" x2="9" y2="4"/><line x1="15" y1="1" x2="15" y2="4"/><line x1="9" y1="20" x2="9" y2="23"/><line x1="15" y1="20" x2="15" y2="23"/><line x1="20" y1="9" x2="23" y2="9"/><line x1="20" y1="14" x2="23" y2="14"/><line x1="1" y1="9" x2="4" y2="9"/><line x1="1" y1="14" x2="4" y2="14"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Bridging Design, Code &amp; AI Tooling</h3>
          <p>
            True velocity happens when design and engineering share the same mental model. I work directly with code-backed prototypes, design tokens, and AI-accelerated workflows to eliminate handoff ambiguity and elevate craft across the entire product lifecycle.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="philosophy-card">
          <div class="philosophy-icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>High Autonomy, High Craft Standards</h3>
          <p>
            Great product work thrives on radical clarity and psychological safety. I run critique focused on intent, logic, and craft rather than subjective preference. I encourage bold exploration while ensuring every detail holds up under intense cross-functional scrutiny.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="philosophy-card philosophy-card-wide">
          <div class="philosophy-icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.4 15a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33 1.82l.06.06a2 2 0 0 1 0 2.83 2 2 0 0 1-2.83 0l-.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82-.33 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1 1.51V21a2 2 0 0 1-2 2 2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 9 19.4a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82.33l-.06.06a2 2 0 0 1-2.83 0 2 2 0 0 1 0-2.83l.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33-1.82 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51-1H3a2 2 0 0 1-2-2 2 2 0 0 1 2-2h.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 4.6 9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33-1.82l-.06-.06a2 2 0 0 1 0-2.83 2 2 0 0 1 2.83 0l.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82.33H9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1-1.51V3a2 2 0 0 1 2-2 2 2 0 0 1 2 2v.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1 1.51 1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82-.33l.06-.06a2 2 0 0 1 2.83 0 2 2 0 0 1 0 2.83l-.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33 1.82V9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.51 1H21a2 2 0 0 1 2 2 2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51 1z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Horizontal Influence &amp; The Product Triad</h3>
          <p>
            Staff-level design is about bringing engineering, product, and operations along on the journey. With my engineering background, I speak the language of technical constraints and trade-offs, helping cross-functional partners see possibilities rather than roadblocks.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Leadership Capabilities Matrix -->
    <section class="competencies-section">
      <div class="section-header-block">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Core Capabilities</span>
        <h2 class="section-heading">Strategic &amp; Technical Competencies</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="competencies-grid">
        <div class="competency-box">
          <h4>Systems &amp; Technical Depth</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Design token architecture &amp; token pipelines</li>
            <li>Production code-backed prototyping (React / Astro)</li>
            <li>Advanced Figma variables, modes &amp; slots</li>
            <li>Hardware &amp; software integration (Retail POS)</li>
            <li>Human-in-the-loop AI interfaces &amp; heuristic QA</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="competency-box">
          <h4>Product Strategy &amp; Growth</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Omnichannel customer journey mapping</li>
            <li>Monetization, margin &amp; conversion optimization</li>
            <li>High-scale loyalty &amp; behavioral mechanics (80M+ members)</li>
            <li>North Star vision &amp; executive alignment</li>
            <li>Multi-year enterprise product roadmapping</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="competency-box">
          <h4>Research Leadership &amp; Influence</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Directing qual &amp; quant research workstreams</li>
            <li>In-store contextual inquiry &amp; field studies</li>
            <li>Telemetry &amp; transaction log triangulation</li>
            <li>Cross-functional alignment (Eng, PM, Store Ops)</li>
            <li>Setting craft quality bars &amp; design critique</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Closing Executive CTA -->
    <section class="about-cta-section">
      <div class="roots-cta-card">
        <h3>Looking for a Principal Designer to tackle complex systems?</h3>
        <p>I’m always open to discussing high-impact product challenges, AI tooling, and systems architecture. Let’s connect.</p>
        <div class="roots-cta-actions">
          <a href="mailto:charlie@charliehv.design" class="btn-primary-about">Get in Touch</a>
          <a href="/" class="btn-secondary-about">Explore Featured Case Studies &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
